<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:zeebe="http://camunda.org/schema/zeebe/1.0" xmlns:modeler="http://camunda.org/schema/modeler/1.0" id="Definitions_ProcessAdherenceEvaluation" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn" exporter="Camunda Modeler" exporterVersion="5.46.1" modeler:executionPlatform="Camunda Cloud" modeler:executionPlatformVersion="8.9.0">
  <bpmn:process id="ProcessAdherenceEvaluation" name="Process Adherence Evaluation" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:documentation>One of the three parallel dimension-scoring processes invoked by ticket-scoring.bpmn's Ticket Scoring call activity. Broken out into its own file/process so each rubric dimension can be deployed and versioned independently. Scores the three Process Adherence categories with evidence and confidence per category. The jiraBugTicket category is mechanically determined already and must be carried through unchanged. Restricted to the get-rubric and lookup-jira-issue tools - the only dimension that needs the Jira lookup.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="StartEvent_ProcessAdherenceEvaluation" name="Start">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_StartToProcessAdherenceEvaluation</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_StartToProcessAdherenceEvaluation" sourceRef="StartEvent_ProcessAdherenceEvaluation" targetRef="AdHocSubProcess_ProcessAdherenceEvaluation" />
    <bpmn:adHocSubProcess id="AdHocSubProcess_ProcessAdherenceEvaluation" name="Process Adherence Evaluation" zeebe:modelerTemplate="io.camunda.connectors.agenticai.aiagent.jobworker.v1" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="7" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
      <bpmn:documentation>Scores the three Process Adherence categories (Jira bug ticket, internal notes, follow-up commitments) with evidence and confidence per category. The jiraBugTicket category is mechanically determined already and must be carried through unchanged. Restricted to the get-rubric and lookup-jira-issue tools - the only dimension that needs the Jira lookup.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.camunda.agenticai:aiagent-job-worker:1" retries="1" />
        <zeebe:adHoc outputCollection="toolCallResults" outputElement="={&#10;  id: toolCall._meta.id,&#10;  name: toolCall._meta.name,&#10;  content: toolCallResult&#10;}" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:input source="openaiCompatible" target="provider.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.LLM_API_ENDPOINT}}" target="provider.openaiCompatible.endpoint" />
          <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.LLM_API_KEY}}" target="provider.openaiCompatible.authentication.apiKey" />
          <zeebe:input source="anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6" target="provider.openaiCompatible.model.model" />
          <zeebe:input source="=&#34;You are a Support QA assessment assistant scoring the Process Adherence dimension of a closed support ticket against the shared QA rubric - call the get-rubric tool first to retrieve the current rubric definitions. Score exactly these three categories: jiraBugTicket, internalNotes, followUpCommitments on the 4-point scale (4-Excellent, 3-Meets Standard, 2-Developing, 1-Does Not Meet), or NotApplicable if a category does not apply to this ticket. The jiraBugTicket category has already been determined mechanically - copy through the provided jiraBugTicketScore for that category unchanged, do not re-score it, and set its evidence to note it was determined mechanically with confidence 1. If a Jira issue is linked you may call the lookup-jira-issue tool to check its status before scoring. For internalNotes and followUpCommitments attach a short evidence string and a confidence level between 0 and 1. Decide whether this ticket shows a process-adherence anomaly (for example a commitment that was not honored, or notes missing at key points). You never assign the final QA rating - your output is a provisional per-category assessment for a Team Lead to review. Your entire response must be a single valid JSON object and nothing else - no markdown code fences, no preamble, no reasoning or explanation before or after it. Begin your response with { and end with }. Use exactly these keys: categoryScores (an object keyed by jiraBugTicket, internalNotes, followUpCommitments - each value an object with score (1-4 or the string NotApplicable), evidence (string), and confidence (0-1)), anomalyFlagged (boolean), and anomalyReasons (array of strings, empty if none).&#34;" target="data.systemPrompt.prompt" />
          <zeebe:input source="=&#34;Ticket &#34; + zendeskTicketId + &#34; - subject: &#34; + ticketSubject + &#34;. Customer: &#34; + customerName + &#34;. Agent: &#34; + agentName + &#34;. Channel: &#34; + channel + &#34; (&#34; + string(replyCount) + &#34; replies, call held: &#34; + string(hasCall) + &#34;).\nThread summary: &#34; + threadExcerpt + &#34;\nDeterministic checks - first response: &#34; + string(firstResponseMinutes) + &#34; min (SLA met: &#34; + string(slaMet) + &#34;), response cadence flagged: &#34; + string(responseCadenceFlag) + &#34;, internal notes present: &#34; + string(internalNotesPresent) + &#34;, follow-up commitment made: &#34; + string(followUpCommitmentMade) + &#34;, follow-up honored on time: &#34; + string(followUpHonoredOnTime) + &#34;, ticket involves a bug: &#34; + string(ticketInvolvesBug) + &#34;, Jira linked: &#34; + string(jiraLinked) + &#34;, Jira issue key: &#34; + jiraIssueKey + &#34;, jiraBugTicket category score (already determined - carry through unchanged): &#34; + string(jiraBugTicketScore) + &#34;.&#34;" target="data.userPrompt.prompt" />
          <zeebe:input target="agentContext" />
          <zeebe:input source="in-process" target="data.memory.storage.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="=10" target="data.memory.contextWindowSize" />
          <zeebe:input source="4" target="data.limits.maxModelCalls" />
          <zeebe:input source="WAIT_FOR_TOOL_CALL_RESULTS" target="data.events.behavior" />
          <zeebe:input source="text" target="data.response.format.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="=true" target="data.response.format.parseJson" />
          <zeebe:input source="=true" target="data.response.includeAssistantMessage" />
          <zeebe:input source="=false" target="data.response.includeAgentContext" />
          <zeebe:input target="agent" />
          <zeebe:output source="=agent" target="agent" />
          <zeebe:output source="=agent.responseJson.categoryScores" target="procCategoryScores" />
          <zeebe:output source="=agent.responseJson.anomalyFlagged" target="procAnomalyFlagged" />
          <zeebe:output source="=agent.responseJson.anomalyReasons" target="procAnomalyReasons" />
          <zeebe:output source="=agent.responseText" target="procResponseText" />
          <zeebe:output source="=agent.responseMessage.metadata.framework.tokenUsage.inputTokenCount" target="procInputTokens" />
          <zeebe:output source="=agent.responseMessage.metadata.framework.tokenUsage.outputTokenCount" target="procOutputTokens" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
        <zeebe:taskHeaders>
          <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateVersion" value="7" />
          <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateId" value="io.camunda.connectors.agenticai.aiagent.jobworker.v1" />
          <zeebe:header key="retryBackoff" value="PT0S" />
        </zeebe:taskHeaders>
        <zeebe:properties>
          <zeebe:property name="io.camunda.agenticai.toolContainer" value="true" />
        </zeebe:properties>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_StartToProcessAdherenceEvaluation</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_ProcessAdherenceEvaluationToEnd</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="Tool_GetRubric_ProcessAdherence" name="Get current rubric">
        <bpmn:documentation>Retrieves the shared QA rubric so the agent scores against the current version, not a hardcoded copy in its prompt.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <zeebe:taskDefinition type="get-rubric" retries="1" />
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="Tool_LookupJiraIssue_ProcessAdherence" name="Look up linked Jira issue">
        <bpmn:documentation>Looks up the status of the Jira issue linked to this ticket (if any), for context when scoring internalNotes/followUpCommitments. Tests controlled, approved tool access to an enterprise system.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <zeebe:taskDefinition type="lookup-jira-issue" retries="1" />
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
    </bpmn:adHocSubProcess>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_ProcessAdherenceEvaluationToEnd" sourceRef="AdHocSubProcess_ProcessAdherenceEvaluation" targetRef="EndEvent_ProcessAdherenceEvaluation" />
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_ProcessAdherenceEvaluation" name="Process adherence scored">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_ProcessAdherenceEvaluationToEnd</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_1">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_1" bpmnElement="ProcessAdherenceEvaluation">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_StartEvent_ProcessAdherenceEvaluation" bpmnElement="StartEvent_ProcessAdherenceEvaluation">
        <dc:Bounds x="142" y="162" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="149" y="205" width="24" height="14" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_AdHocSubProcess_ProcessAdherenceEvaluation" bpmnElement="AdHocSubProcess_ProcessAdherenceEvaluation" isExpanded="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="220" y="80" width="360" height="200" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Tool_GetRubric_ProcessAdherence" bpmnElement="Tool_GetRubric_ProcessAdherence">
        <dc:Bounds x="345" y="115" width="110" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Tool_LookupJiraIssue_ProcessAdherence" bpmnElement="Tool_LookupJiraIssue_ProcessAdherence">
        <dc:Bounds x="345" y="195" width="110" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_EndEvent_ProcessAdherenceEvaluation" bpmnElement="EndEvent_ProcessAdherenceEvaluation">
        <dc:Bounds x="652" y="162" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="626" y="205" width="89" height="27" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_StartToProcessAdherenceEvaluation" bpmnElement="Flow_StartToProcessAdherenceEvaluation">
        <di:waypoint x="178" y="180" />
        <di:waypoint x="220" y="180" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_ProcessAdherenceEvaluationToEnd" bpmnElement="Flow_ProcessAdherenceEvaluationToEnd">
        <di:waypoint x="580" y="180" />
        <di:waypoint x="652" y="180" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
